(A loop body runs only on some paths, like a branch: a text declared in it
 under the name of a top-level buffer lasts as long as the body, and after
 the loop the name is the top-level buffer again.)
a buffer called hold is "abc".

To 'grow' with a buffer called data.
    For each k from 1 to 3000, append "abcdefgh" to data.

To 'looper'.
    For each n from 1 to 2,
        a text called hold is "local {n}",
        Print "in loop {hold}".
    'grow' of hold.
    Print "after loop {hold's size}".

'looper'.
Print "top {hold's size}".
